  "slug": "artist:namie-amuro",
  "name": "Namie Amuro",
  "editorial_article": "Namie Amuro made her professional debut in 1992 as the lead singer of the group Super Monkey's under the Toshiba EMI label. In 1995, she transitioned to a solo career with the single 'Taiyou no Season' and subsequently released her debut solo album, 'Dance Tracks Vol.1', which topped the Oricon weekly chart and sold over 2,000,000 copies. Following a move to the Avex Trax label, she achieved massive commercial success with her 1996 album 'Sweet 19 Blues', which sold over 3 million units in Japan. Her 1997 single 'Can You Celebrate?' became the best-selling single by a female solo artist in Japanese chart history. Amuro's later discography includes projects like 'Queen of Hip-Pop' and the 2008 greatest hits compilation 'Best Fiction', which spent six consecutive weeks at number one on the Oricon charts. Her work with collaborators like Verbal and M-Flo on the Suite Chic project marked a notable shift in her musical scope during her multi-decade career.",
